	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Gratiam et pacem a domino per Iesum Christum.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z3"/>Valde sane sum recreatus, quando intellexi me, hominem <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>plane nihili quasique terre vermiculum<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Ps 22 (Vulg. 21), 7</ref></cit>.</note>, ei viro curae <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>esse,<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Ein entsprechender Brief <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> ist nicht überliefert.</note> qui hodie inter christiane doctos aut primarius <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>est omnino aut paucos admodum pares habet.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z7"/>Iesus Christus istum charitatis adfectum in te semper <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>conservet atque etiam adaugeat,<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Vgl. Petrus <hi>Venerabilis,</hi> Epistulae, 42: "Conservet in vobis et adaugeat hunc caritatis affectum vera caritas deus".</note> donec in perfectum <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>virum illum adoleveris<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Eph 4, 13</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Jak 3, 2</ref></cit>.</note>.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Itaque supersum adhuc, <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>antistes venerande, neque me simul cum meis <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>tollere voluit dominus, nimirum ut partem adhuc <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>aliquam laborum exanthlarem, qui ecclesiam Christi <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>in hac cruenta atque mortali harena militantem<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Vgl. Adagia, 1, 9, 83 (<bibl>ASD</bibl> II/2 396, Nr. 883).</note> <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>exercent, quamquam longe<pb type="edition" next="107"/> prętulissem cum meis <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>obdormire<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>2Kor 5, 8</ref></cit>.</note>.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Sed domino non ita visum est, qui <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>qum etiam capitis nostri capillos numeratos habeat,<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Mt 10, 30 par</ref></cit>.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>nihil circa nos agit perficitque sine miranda <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>ac aeternum nobis adoranda providentia.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Ei igitur <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>sit honos et gloria et gratiarum actio<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8"><cit type="bible"><ref>Apk 4, 9</ref></cit>.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Porro <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>inter meos, quorum obdormitionis in domino memini, <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>est et <persName ref="p5530">Iacobus Kriech</persName><note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="9">Siehe oben <ref target="file12116">Nr. 2069</ref>, 9-22 und Anm. 7. Zu <persName ref="p8031">Béat Comtes</persName> Trauer über den Tod von <persName ref="p5530">Jakob Kriech</persName> s. auch <persName ref="p8031">Comtes</persName> Briefe an <persName ref="p8011">Gwalther</persName> vom 18. Dezember 1544 (Zürich ZB, Ms F 38, 215; gedruckt in: Corr. des réformateurs IX 419, <ref target="file11466">Nr. 1423</ref>) und vom 24. Januar 1545 (Zürich ZB, Ms F 38, 216).</note>, iuvenis ille <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinus</placeName>, quem <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>tu mihi tam studiose commendaras,<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Siehe <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl>, <ref target="file11956">Nr. 1909</ref>.</note> quemque ego tam <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>solerter et officiose enutriendum instituendumque <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>curabam<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11"><persName ref="p8031">Comte</persName> hatte <persName ref="p5530">Jakob Kriech</persName> Unterricht erteilt; s. oben <ref target="file12116">Nr. 2069</ref>, 14f.</note>.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Quare te vehementer oro, ut, quando <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>illę etiam sunt tuę partes, iuvenis ipsius patrem <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>reliquosque eius adfines consoleris;<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="12">Zu <persName ref="p8031">Comtes</persName> Bitten betreffend den Vater von <persName ref="p5530">Jakob Kriech</persName> s. auch <persName ref="p8031">Comtes</persName> Brief an <persName ref="p8011">Gwalther</persName> vom 18. Dezember 1544 (wie oben Anm. 9).</note> set iam de eo <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>non sinit dolor plura scribere.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Responsionem tuam <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>secundam ad <persName ref="p8312">Cochlęum</persName><note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> "Brevis <foreign xml:lang="el">ἀντιβολή</foreign>", erschienen im Dezember 1544; s. <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl> <ref target="file12057">[Nr. 2010]</ref> 460, Anm. 22. - Seine erste Schrift gegen <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> hatte <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> bereits im Frühjahr 1544 nach <placeName ref="l280">Lausanne</placeName> geschickt; s. <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl> 232, 27f und Anm. 7. 233.</note> legam tam avide, quam <lb xml:id="p1z29"/>vehementer demirari soleo tua omnia scripta; <lb xml:id="p1z30"/>deinde ad te rescribam, quod mihi de utraque<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Gemeint sind beide Schriften <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> gegen <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>; s. oben Anm. 13.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z31"/>dabit dominus.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Interea valde cupio priorem librum<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15">Die erste Schrift von <persName ref="p8312">Johannes Cochläus</persName> gegen <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName>, die unter dem Titel "De canonicae scripturae et catholicae ecclesiae autoritate" 1543 erschienen war; s. <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl>, <ref target="file11885">Nr. 1839</ref>, Anm. 2.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z32"/>ac replicam<note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16"><persName ref="p8312">Johannes Cochläus</persName>' zweite Schrift gegen <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> mit dem Titel "Replica brevis", gedruckt im Spätsommer 1544; s. <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl> <ref target="file12046">[Nr. 1999]</ref> 429f, Anm. 12.</note> <persName ref="p8312">Cochlęi</persName> ad te videre, ut hinc inde <lb xml:id="p1z33"/>rebus diligentius collatis maiorem postea <lb xml:id="p1z34"/>fructum ex lectione tuorum scriptorum possim <lb xml:id="p1z35"/>colligere.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Id ergo tu in meam gratiam curabis, <lb xml:id="p1z36"/>ut hic meus tabellarius<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Der junge Jakob [...], der auch <persName ref="p714">Curiones</persName> Brief vom 18. Januar 1545 überbrachte; s. oben <ref target="file12116">Nr. 2069</ref>, 4-6. 99f.</note> libros illos ad me <lb xml:id="p1z37"/>ferat, cui etiam iniunxi, ut prętium numeraret.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><pb type="scan" next="2808v."/><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Quod autem petis, ut in <placeName ref="l832">Gallicum</placeName> transmutem sermonem,<note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18">Siehe oben <ref target="file12116">Nr. 2069</ref>, 48-68.</note> <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>quę tu <placeName ref="l822">Germanice</placeName> de coena domini scribis ad <persName ref="p1974">Lutherum</persName>,<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19">Das "Warhaffte Bekanntnuß" der <placeName ref="l587">Zürcher</placeName>, das kurz vordem 12. März 1545 erschien; s. oben <ref target="file12108">Nr. 2061</ref>, Anm. 9, und unten <ref target="file12143">Nr. 2096</ref>-2103.</note> <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>valde gaudeo; nihil enim perinde cupio, quam scripta <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>tua omnia, vere pia et docta, pluribus <lb xml:id="p2z5"/>innotescere, quamquam illud non negligendum censeo, <lb xml:id="p2z6"/>quis sit <persName ref="p1974">Lutherus</persName>, qui mores nostri seculi, quę molimina <lb xml:id="p2z7"/>principum, qui rerumpublicarum status, quam varii et <lb xml:id="p2z8"/>differentes sensus eorum, qui etiam de cognita <lb xml:id="p2z9"/>evangelii veritate<pb type="edition" next="108"/> gloriantur: unus ait, alius <lb xml:id="p2z10"/>negat, at tertius ponendum censet in deliberatione<note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20">Vgl. <hi><persName ref="p18901">Terenz</persName>,</hi> Phormio, 2, 3. Vgl. ferner <hi><persName ref="p18722">Erasmus</persName>,</hi> Lingua (<bibl>ASD</bibl> IV/I 346, 921-923): "quemadmodum apud Terentium faciunt tres advocati, quorum unus ait rescindi posse, alter negat, tertius deliberandum amplius censet".</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z11"/>Quare summam puto adhibendam cautionem in hoc toto <lb xml:id="p2z12"/>tractando negotio, pręsertim quum eius sit <lb xml:id="p2z13"/>momenti, ut aeque magni nullum reperias hodie <lb xml:id="p2z14"/>in tota republica christiana.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Verum hęc omnia <lb xml:id="p2z15"/>prudentię tuę singularique iudicio commissa sunto.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell"><lb xml:id="p2z16"/>Vale beate atque bene, antistes mihi semper <lb xml:id="p2z17"/>observande.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l280">Lausannę</placeName>, 9. calendas februarii 1545.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z18"/>Tuus ex voto <lb xml:id="p2z19"/><persName ref="p8031">B. Comes Donzarensis</persName><note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21"><placeName ref="l2146">Donzère</placeName> (<placeName ref="l3647">Dép. Drôme</placeName>, <placeName ref="l832">Frankreich</placeName>).</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la" ana="salute"><lb xml:id="p2z20"/>Doctrina atque pietate semper <lb xml:id="p2z21"/>mirandos symmistas tuos omnes <lb xml:id="p2z22"/>saluto in domino.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf f. 2808a,v.:]</note>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p4z1"/>Doctissimo gravissimoque et <lb xml:id="p4z2"/>vigilantissimo ecclesię <lb xml:id="p4z3"/><placeName ref="l587">Tigurinę</placeName> episcopo, <lb xml:id="p4z4"/>d. <persName ref="p495">Heynricho Bullingero</persName>, <lb xml:id="p4z5"/>viro ac domino mihi semper <lb xml:id="p4z6"/>colendo.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
	</text>
